<title>USA: Pages Q1 shr loss $0.04 vs profit $0.62.</title>
<headline>Pages Q1 shr loss $0.04 vs profit $0.62.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr		  loss $     0.04  profit $	0.62</p>
<p> Net		  loss    239,626  profit   3,566,927</p>
<p> Revs			 7,144,194	     9,457,068</p>
<p>Common/common shr</p>
<p>equivalents</p>
<p> outstanding	     6,199,000	     5,721,000</p>
<p>Note: Income for first quarter of 1997 included a non-cash reduction of expense of $431,287 to record the current value of Stock Appreciation Rights issued in 1996. Income for the first quarter of 1996 includes recognition of a $3,255,337 gain from the sale of the company's United Kingdom distribution channel.  Also included in the income for the first quarter of 1996, from discontinued operations of CA Short Co, was a $994,664 increase in income from cumulative effect of a change in accounting principle.</p>
<p>Full company name is Pages Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 259-1610))</p>
